course: dictionary
lesson: 11565
title: Anchorage: three meanings in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one you need. Anchorage has three. A capital letter in the middle of a sentence is a clue: Anchorage, with a capital A, is a city.
explain: «The little boat rode safely in the anchorage, away from the storm.» The clues are boat, safely and storm. A boat drops its anchor in calm, sheltered water, so here an anchorage is a sheltered place where ships can stop. Swap the meaning in: "the boat rode safely in the sheltered place where ships drop anchor" still makes sense.
explain: «The child seat clicks into the anchorage in the back of the car.» The clues are child seat and car. This anchorage is a strong point that the seat is fixed to, so it holds things steady. «Anchorage is surrounded by mountains in Alaska» uses a capital A, so it is a name: a city.
fact: An anchorage is a place where ships can safely drop anchor, usually calm, sheltered water.
fact: «A safe anchorage» means a calm, sheltered place where a boat can stay still.
fact: Anchorage, with a capital A, is the largest city in the US state of Alaska.
fact: An anchorage can also be a strong point that something is fixed to, such as a car seat or a bridge cable.
fact: Ports grew up near good anchorages, because ships needed a safe place to wait.
exercise: «The ships waited in the sheltered anchorage until the storm passed.» What is an anchorage here? | A kind of sail | A tall tower on the coast | A loud storm | *A calm place where ships can safely drop anchor
exercise: «Anchorage is a city surrounded by mountains in Alaska.» What does the capital A tell you? | *Anchorage is a name, the city in Alaska | It means the same as a harbour | It means a strong rope | It starts a new sentence only
exercise: «The seat belt is fixed to a strong anchorage in the car.» What is the anchorage? | A seat that folds down | *A strong point the belt is fixed to | A kind of wheel | A road sign
test: «Ports grew up near good anchorages, where ships could rest safely.» Which phrase is closest in meaning to anchorage here? | Steep hill | Busy shop | *Sheltered harbour | Open field
test: Mia says the city Anchorage and an anchorage are the same thing. What is the answer? | Yes, they always mean a city | No, one of them is a fish | *No, the capital A means a name; the other word means a sheltered place or a fixing point | Yes, and both are in Alaska
exam: Which sentence uses anchorage to mean a strong fixing point? | «The anchorage was full of fishing boats in the morning.» | «The anchorage was a sunny day at the seaside.» | *«The climber tied the rope to a strong anchorage on the rock.» | «Anchorage is famous for snow and long summer days.»
